1
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:09,529
Some lines you just have to cross.

2
00:12:07,058 --> 00:12:13,058
Little Woods is a drama, thriller film directed by Nia DaCosta.

3
00:18:10,588 --> 00:18:16,588
For years, Ollie has illicitly helped the struggling residents of her North
Dakota oil boomtown access Canadian health care and medication.

4
00:24:14,117 --> 00:24:20,117
When the authorities catch on, she plans to abandon her crusade, only to be
dragged in even deeper after a desperate plea for help from her sister.

5
00:30:17,647 --> 00:30:23,647
Oleander 'Ollie' Hale, played by Tessa Thompson.

6
00:36:21,176 --> 00:36:27,176
Deborah Hale, played by Lily James.

7
00:42:24,705 --> 00:42:30,705
Bill, played by Luke Kirby.

8
00:48:28,235 --> 00:48:34,235
Ian, played by James Badge Dale.

9
00:54:31,764 --> 00:54:37,764
Carter, played by Lance Reddick.

10
01:00:35,294 --> 01:00:41,294
Jenny, played by Elizabeth Maxwell.

11
01:06:38,823 --> 01:06:44,823
Little Woods is a 2018 crime drama film, written and directed by
Nia DaCosta in her feature directorial debut.

12
01:12:42,352 --> 01:12:48,352
The film stars Tessa Thompson, Lily James, Luke Kirby,
James Badge Dale and Lance Reddick.

13
01:18:45,882 --> 01:18:51,882
Little Woods had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on 21 April 2018, and was released on 19 April
2019 in the United States by Neon and on 16 May 2019 in Australia by Limelight Distribution.

14
01:24:49,411 --> 01:24:55,411
In the United Kingdom, it was released both digitally and on DVD as
Crossing the Line on 29 April 2019 by Signature Entertainment.

15
01:30:52,941 --> 01:30:58,941
The film explores themes of canada, health care, north
dakota, prescription medication, abortion.

16
01:36:56,470 --> 01:37:02,470
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
